# HireSense AI — example environment file. Copy this to ".env" (same folder
# as manage.py) and replace the placeholders with your real values.
# .env is gitignored, so your secrets never end up in the repo.
#
# InsForge auth (see the README's "InsForge auth" section). The React
# app signs users in against InsForge; Django verifies the tokens.
# INSFORGE_AUTH_ENABLED=true switches the API on to dual-auth
# (sessions + Bearer); INSFORGE_AUTH_REQUIRED=true as well makes the
# API Bearer-only. The frontend needs its own pair at BUILD time —
# VITE_INSFORGE_URL + VITE_INSFORGE_ANON_KEY in frontend/.env (same
# URL, the project's public anon key). Leave all of these unset and
# the API stays session-only (the HTML pages always are).
# INSFORGE_AUTH_ENABLED=true
# INSFORGE_AUTH_REQUIRED=false
# INSFORGE_BASE_URL=https://<appkey>.us-east.insforge.app
#
# Supabase Postgres (see the README's "Supabase Postgres" section).
# Leave this empty to keep using SQLite (the default, zero-setup).
# Set it to your OWN fresh Supabase project's connection string to use
# Postgres instead. NEVER point this at the live Next.js app's project
# — the two apps must never share tables or data.
# Prefer the transaction pooler form (port 6543); the direct form
# (port 5432) also works. Add ?sslmode=require if your copied string
# doesn't already include it — Supabase requires SSL.
# Example shape (yours will differ — never paste a real password here):
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres.<ref>:<password>@aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres?sslmode=require
DATABASE_URL=
#
# Groq AI (see the README's "Groq AI" section). Leave empty to keep
# using the deterministic fallbacks only (keyword criteria draft,
# question bank, checklist scorer). Set it to switch on AI criteria
# drafting, AI interview questions (JD + company + track + difficulty),
# and AI answer feedback. Scores stay deterministic either way.
# Get a key at console.groq.com. GROQ_MODEL is optional.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=llama-3.3-70b-versatile
#
# Gemini AI, second provider alongside Groq (see the README's
# "AI providers" section). Leave empty to skip Gemini. Set it, with or
# without GROQ_API_KEY, to let the app answer AI calls with Gemini.
# Get a key at aistudio.google.com. GEMINI_MODEL is optional.
# AI_PROVIDER pins one provider ("groq" or "gemini"); unset means Groq
# first if its key is set, else Gemini.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.0-flash
# AI_PROVIDER=
